After real reset and before exposure, host_trace checks exact inherited BaseAdapter.checked/JsonLineAdapter._exchange and the reviewed WslAimPluginAdapter type. It installs reversible instance observers for these methods, original bounded queue put/get, and WSL proxy stdin/stdout delegates. Each original bound implementation receives exactly the original arguments once, its original result/exception is passed through. No validator, packet, math, clock, source identity, deadline or standard-library json function is replaced. The json_adapter module's temporary json name delegates to the actual original module, observing only that caller's existing act dumps; all other loads/dumps pass directly through. It is restored after owned cleanup.

Hot path stores at most64 scalar events under a short in-memory lock and one exact immutable bytes reference passed to the real enqueue attempt; there is no hot parse/hash/file IO. After original resources close, all hooks are restored, then one daemon evidence writer with a100ms join saves HOST_ACTUAL_IO_TRACE.json and calculates the actual enqueue-argument bytes/SHA/original six identity. Queue put failure is distinguished by enqueue_completed=false. This SHA is no longer a reconstruction. It proves the bytes supplied to original queue put, **not full OS write or Linux delivery**. A successful original FileIO.write return n is counted; a blocked/error write may already have partially entered the OS, so zero return count never proves zero delivered bytes. stdout readline and queue receive retain actual enter/end/error times; no late response is read additionally or accepted.

If artifact IO is blocked/failed or the original IO thread is unfinished, completeness is unknown and resource result fails accordingly. Evidence write budget is after resource close, not a new authority/capture deadline. Peer signal/finally behavior is identical to the frozen candidate. The repaired generic worker belongs to the other agent; this directory never edits it, and fresh registration binds its then-current real source hashes.

Queue linearization occurs inside the original put operation. Its worker can start writing before the caller's put-end record; this is ordinary concurrent ordering, not a negative transport interval or a fabricated enqueue timestamp. Host records use the same unchanged perf_counter as the original host authority. Foreign Linux/ROS clock numbers remain separate.

